### Library-Specific: Zod with Transform

Source: https://github.com/react-hook-form/resolvers/blob/master/_autodocs/configuration.md

Use zodResolver with a transformed Zod schema. When the transform changes the output type, you must specify all three generics (input, unknown, output) in useForm to maintain type safety.

```typescript
const schema = z.object({
  date: z.string().pipe(z.coerce.date()),
  count: z.string().pipe(z.coerce.number())
}).transform(data => ({
  ...data,
  timestamp: data.date.getTime()
}));

// Must specify all three generics when transforms change output type
useForm<z.input<typeof schema>, unknown, z.output<typeof schema>>({
  resolver: zodResolver(schema)
});
```

--------------------------------

### Zod resolver with type inference

Source: https://github.com/react-hook-form/resolvers/blob/master/README.md

Example of using zodResolver with react-hook-form. Shows automatic type inference from the schema and how to force the output type with explicit generics.

```tsx
import { useForm } from 'react-hook-form';
import { zodResolver } from '@hookform/resolvers/zod';
import { z } from 'zod'; // or 'zod/v4'

const schema = z.object({
  id: z.number(),
});

// Automatically infers the output type from the schema
useForm({
  resolver: zodResolver(schema),
});

// Force the output type
useForm<z.input<typeof schema>, any, z.output<typeof schema>>({
  resolver: zodResolver(schema),
});
```

--------------------------------

### Basic usage with Zod v3/v4

Source: https://github.com/react-hook-form/resolvers/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/zod-resolver.md

Example of using zodResolver with a Zod schema in a react-hook-form form, including error rendering.

```typescript
import { useForm } from 'react-hook-form';
import { zodResolver } from '@hookform/resolvers/zod';
import { z } from 'zod';

const schema = z.object({
  name: z.string().min(2, { message: 'Name must be at least 2 characters' }),
  email: z.string().email({ message: 'Invalid email' }),
  age: z.number().min(18, { message: 'Must be 18 or older' })
});

const { register, handleSubmit, formState: { errors } } = useForm({
  resolver: zodResolver(schema),
  mode: 'onBlur'
});

return (
  <form onSubmit={handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>
    <input {...register('name')} />
    {errors.name && <span>{errors.name.message}</span>}

    <input type="email" {...register('email')} />
    {errors.email && <span>{errors.email.message}</span>}

    <input type="number" {...register('age')} />
    {errors.age && <span>{errors.age.message}</span>}

    <button type="submit">Submit</button>
  </form>
);
```

### TypeScript

Source: https://github.com/react-hook-form/resolvers/blob/master/README.md

Most of the resolvers can infer the output type from the schema. See comparison table for more details.

```tsx
useForm<Input, Context, Output>()
```

Example:

```tsx
import { useForm } from 'react-hook-form';
import { zodResolver } from '@hookform/resolvers/zod';
import { z } from 'zod'; // or 'zod/v4'

const schema = z.object({
  id: z.number(),
});

// Automatically infers the output type from the schema
useForm({
  resolver: zodResolver(schema),
});

// Force the output type
useForm<z.input<typeof schema>, any, z.output<typeof schema>>({
  resolver: zodResolver(schema),
});
```

--------------------------------

### Type Inference

Source: https://github.com/react-hook-form/resolvers/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/zod-resolver.md

### Type Inference

The Zod resolver automatically infers types when used without explicit generics:

```typescript
const schema = z.object({ name: z.string() });

// Types are inferred automatically
const { handleSubmit } = useForm({
  resolver: zodResolver(schema)
  // Input type: { name: string }
  // Output type: { name: string }
});
```

With transformations that change types:

```typescript
const schema = z.object({
  count: z.string().pipe(z.coerce.number()) // Input is string, output is number
});

// Explicit generics needed to distinguish input/output
useForm<z.input<typeof schema>, any, z.output<typeof schema>>({
  resolver: zodResolver(schema)
});
```

