### Type Inference

Source: https://github.com/react-hook-form/resolvers/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/zod-resolver.md

### Type Inference

The Zod resolver automatically infers types when used without explicit generics:

```typescript
const schema = z.object({ name: z.string() });

// Types are inferred automatically
const { handleSubmit } = useForm({
  resolver: zodResolver(schema)
  // Input type: { name: string }
  // Output type: { name: string }
});
```

With transformations that change types:

```typescript
const schema = z.object({
  count: z.string().pipe(z.coerce.number()) // Input is string, output is number
});

// Explicit generics needed to distinguish input/output
useForm<z.input<typeof schema>, any, z.output<typeof schema>>({
  resolver: zodResolver(schema)
});
```

